<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Governorate of New Toledo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1534–1542</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">Governorate</a> of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> was the territory granted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-de-almagro">Diego de Almagro</a> in 1534, lying south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro">Francisco Pizarro</a>'s New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>. Its vague northern boundary and the dispute over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a> led to civil war between the conquerors and Almagro's execution in 1538. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-laws">New Laws of 1542</a> replaced it with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-peru">Viceroyalty of Peru</a>.</p></div>
<p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/state/governorate-of-new-toledo">State page: history, lineage and connections &rarr;</a></p>
